  "summary": "Four preprints propose dark-sector models and model-independent consistency tests targeting cosmological tensions and degeneracies among dark components.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is probing the dark sector through either extended models or consistency relations. Kinessence combines K-mouflage with quintessence to yield phantom crossing and sign-switching dark energy, assessed against background and CMB observables. Two other items emphasize tests: the 0i Einstein equation is used for three model-independent, observable-only tests to break degeneracies among gravity, dark energy and dark matter, and a universal ratio R=(1+z_t)/(1+z_pk)=1.1596 links the onset of acceleration to the fσ8 turnover in flat ΛCDM. A further paper argues that neutrino self-interactions from renormalizable theories imply resonant mediator behavior, altering the Boltzmann hierarchy and the CMB ΔN_eff. These are distinct approaches, but each offers a route to discriminating dark-sector physics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
